+### Actual isolated guest resource route
+
+`reims-vgpu-c/tests/cpu_shadow_core.rs` compiles and runs
+`tests/c/cpu_shadow_core.c` against the actual C library on Linux with an arm64
+guest ABI. The adjacent Python generator uses the suite's independent authored
+guest ABI builders to write a build-only C header. It contains no recorded
+guest payload or Apple shader and can also be compiled into an Android fixture.
+
+```sh
+cargo test -p reims-vgpu-c --no-default-features \
+  --features vulkan,guest-arm64 --test cpu_shadow_core -- --nocapture
+```
+
+Run it without concurrent GPU or guest boot work. Each child process explicitly
+selects CPU-shadow before device creation, has a fresh shader cache, bounds
+each stamp wait and has a process deadline. It creates ordinary sealed memfd
+RAM through `RvgDeviceConfig.memory_files`, closes its original descriptor, and
+drives only the public C API and MMIO registers. The actual FIFO device-info
+query must show the range-buffer/shared-heap gates and respect the argument
+buffer configuration, tested both enabled and disabled. An isolated task must
+copy and write a private-flag buffer and a shared heap's placed buffer, then
+discard both parents and reuse the same references over newly fragmented page
+table backing. Exact comparisons cover the output, every old and new data page
+and each physical gap; no synchronization flags copy a private buffer back on
+the test's behalf. Task deletion must complete, and the existing diagnostic
+query must report completed real CPU-shadow epochs and changed ordinary RAM.
+
+This reaches core's resource constructors and the task's capability handshake,
+which the platform-only buffer/heap examples do not reach. It does not run a
+guest framework's argument-buffer shaders or attest a cold boot, native iOS
+thread-pointer swap path, exact final package, or APK.
